summary: 'Round-2 team panel attacked the 6 swarm problems with concrete fixes AND the recursive "make ourselves better" angle. Key reframe (Jinx, verified at cli.ts:89 = "weave write not implemented; Phase 1 read-only"): 4 of 6 fixes defend a WRITE PATH THAT DOESN''T EXIST, so they are DESIGN-CONSTRAINTS on the write-path build, not parallel features to build now. Corrected critical path: fix absorb concurrency → build the write path (weave/consolidate/GAP-7) → build the N≥3 same-feature CONTENDED fixture → MEASURE labor_ratio vs git. Self-improvement claims are only real with FALSIFIABLE ARTIFACTS (blind human-scored red-team for injection; a logged agent decision changed by an intent-board read) — else calibration-of-the-calibrator.'
